        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div style="margin-top: 16px;">
          <h3>Is ZYN or Nordic Spirit stronger?</h3>
          <p>Nordic Spirit starts at a higher minimum strength (6 mg vs ZYN's 1.5 mg) and reaches up to 13 mg in some markets. ZYN offers a wider range from 1.5 mg to 11 mg, making it better for both light and moderate users. Neither brand targets the ultra-strong segment.</p>

          <h3>Which tastes better, ZYN or Nordic Spirit?</h3>
          <p>ZYN favours subtle, clean flavours designed for all-day use. Nordic Spirit offers more distinctive profiles -- Bergamot Wildberry and Elderflower are unique to the category. If you value nuance, try Nordic Spirit. If you prefer consistency, start with ZYN.</p>

          <h3>Are ZYN and Nordic Spirit both Swedish?</h3>
          <p>Yes. ZYN is made by Swedish Match (now owned by Philip Morris International) and Nordic Spirit is made by JTI (Japan Tobacco International). Both brands originate from Sweden's long nicotine pouch tradition.</p>

          <h3>Why is Nordic Spirit's can different?</h3>
          <p>Nordic Spirit uses a tall, cylindrical can instead of the traditional flat round design. It is a deliberate premium positioning choice -- the matte finish, muted earth tones, and minimal branding are designed to stand out on shelves and appeal to design-conscious consumers.</p>

          <h3>Which is better for beginners?</h3>
          <p>ZYN is the better choice for beginners because it offers lower strength options starting at 1.5 mg. Nordic Spirit's lowest strength is typically 6 mg, which may be too intense for someone new to nicotine pouches.</p>

          <h3>Can I buy both brands from SnusFriend?</h3>
